<title>NETHERLANDS: FORECAST - Dutch Nov CPI seen up 2.4 pct y/y.</title>
<headline>FORECAST - Dutch Nov CPI seen up 2.4 pct y/y.</headline>
<dateline>AMSTERDAM 1996-12-05</dateline>
<text>
<p>Bank economists, on average, expected Dutch November consumer price inflation to remain unchanged at a year-on-year rate of 2.4 percent from October, according to a Reuters survey.</p>
<p>November CPI data are due at 0930 GMT on Friday. Economists' forecasts are summarised below:</p>
<p> GMT   Date  Period   Indicator	   Consensus   Range   Pvs</p>
<p> 0930  6/12  Nov	CPI mth/mth	   unch    +0.1/-0.1 +0.3</p>
<p> 0930  6/12  Nov	CPI yr/yr	   +2.4 pct  +2.5/+2.3 +2.4</p>
<p>Forecasts contributed by: ABN AMRO, ING, Generale Bank, MeesPierson and Rabobank.</p>
<p>-- Amsterdam newsroom +31 20 504 5000, Fax +31 20 504 5040</p>
